    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. There's exactly one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it now passes with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the registration year), following the same pattern the codebase already uses for other derived read-only owner fields like `displayName` and `initials`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` response schema (so the openapi-generator produces the field on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` guarantees two-digit zero-padding, matching the `SMI-0007-M26` example.\n\nThe value is derived purely from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, so no entity/DB changes were needed. The `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test and the full suite are green.",
